---
/**
 * /wallpapers/gym — SEO landing page for the Gym / fitness category.
 * Chrome page (ChromeLayout), fully indexable, links through to the real
 * photos at /gallery#stoic (the "Gym" world's slug — display name only
 * changed 2026-09-10, see BUILD_LOG.md).
 */
import ChromeLayout from '../../layouts/ChromeLayout.astro';
---

<ChromeLayout
  title="Gym & Fitness Motivational Wallpapers | motivationalwallpaper.com"
  description="Discipline and workout motivation wallpapers for iPhone lock screens"
>
  <h1>Gym & Fitness Motivational Wallpapers</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Wallpapers built for the days motivation doesn't show up on its own.
  </p>

  <p>
    Discipline in the gym rarely comes from feeling inspired — it comes from
    a system that doesn't depend on how you feel that morning. These gym and
    fitness wallpapers are designed to sit on your lock screen as a quiet,
    repeated cue: the work is the point, whether or not anyone's watching.
    Every time you check your phone before a lift, a run, or a set you'd
    rather skip, the wallpaper is there first.
  </p>
  <p>
    This category leans into resolve rather than hype — dark, steel-toned
    backdrops with short, direct lines instead of loud gym-poster slogans.
    The goal isn't a burst of energy that fades by lunchtime; it's a small,
    daily reminder that shows up on your phone as often as you do, so
    showing up for your training becomes the default instead of the
    exception. Whether you're chasing a specific goal — a lift number, a
    race, a body you're rebuilding — or just trying to stay consistent
    through a long stretch of ordinary training days, these wallpapers are
    built to back you up on the days the motivation genuinely runs out.
  </p>

  <p class="cta">
    <a href="/gallery#stoic">Browse the Gym wallpapers &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</ChromeLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--t-title1-size);
    font-weight: var(--t-title1-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--t-title1-track);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--t-lead-size);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .cta {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cta a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
